{"title":"Hydrogeologist Roadmap","role":"Hydrogeologist","summary":"A Hydrogeologist studies the occurrence, movement, quality, recharge and sustainable use of groundwater. The role combines geology, hydrology, hydrochemistry, field investigation, GIS, remote sensing, groundwater modelling and water-resource management.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc. — Geology / Earth Science"},"about":[{"label":"Career-route check","text":"B.Sc. Geology/Earth Science is a strong academic foundation. However, many specialist Hydrogeologist positions—particularly government, consulting and senior technical roles—may require or prefer a relevant M.Sc./M.Tech. in Geology, Applied Geology, Hydrogeology, Hydrology or a related discipline."}],"intro":[{"type":"table","header":["Item","Roadmap"],"rows":[[{"text":"Starts"},{"text":"Year 1 UG · 2026"}],[{"text":"Degree"},{"text":"B.Sc."}],[{"text":"Course"},{"text":"Geology / Earth Science"}],[{"text":"Target career"},{"text":"Hydrogeologist"}],[{"text":"Primary domains"},{"text":"Groundwater, hydrogeology, hydrology, hydrochemistry"}],[{"text":"Core field skills"},{"text":"Geological mapping, groundwater surveys, well assessment, sampling"}],[{"text":"Digital skills"},{"text":"GIS, remote sensing, groundwater modelling, Python"}],[{"text":"Typical entry"},{"text":"Hydrogeology Trainee / Junior Hydrogeologist / Geologist"}],[{"text":"Long-term roles"},{"text":"Hydrogeologist → Senior Hydrogeologist → Principal Hydrogeologist / Project Lead"}]]}],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Geology trainee, field assistant, groundwater trainee, GIS/environmental roles"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Hydrogeology, hydrochemistry, groundwater modelling, GIS or water resources"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Senior Hydrogeologist, Groundwater Specialist, Project Hydrogeologist"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain rele